<title>SRI LANKA: Pure Beverages jumps on news strike over.</title>
<headline>Pure Beverages jumps on news strike over.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Pure Beverages Co Ltd rose 21.43 percent or 4.50 rupees to 25.50 on news that an 11-week strike at two bottling plants will end on Friday, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Investors are reacting to news that the strike which crippled the supply of Coca-Cola will end soon,&quot; said a local broker.</p>
<p>More than 700 workers were on strike at two bottling plants run by Pure Beverages Co Ltd, the island's sole local bottler of Coca-Cola and a 51 percent subsidiary of Singapore's Fraser &amp; Neave, Coke's regional bottler.</p>
<p>--Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
